WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.118
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEIC preparation.

2
00:00:05.418 --> 00:00:08.839
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.139 --> 00:00:17.631
Unit ten: Listening Review: Paraphrase and Distractors. Today you will recognise paraphrase and avoid the most common listening traps.

4
00:00:17.931 --> 00:00:20.700
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.633 --> 00:00:24.901
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:26.937
Paraphrase.

7
00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:30.855
Paraphrase means the same idea in different words.

8
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:33.275
The answer is a paraphrase.

9
00:00:33.883 --> 00:00:36.280
Your turn. Say: Paraphrase.

10
00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:40.343
Paraphrase.

11
00:00:41.083 --> 00:00:42.177
Distractor.

12
00:00:43.183 --> 00:00:46.019
Distractor means a wrong answer that sounds possible.

13
00:00:46.617 --> 00:00:48.581
This option is a distractor.

14
00:00:49.183 --> 00:00:51.743
Your turn. Say: Distractor.

15
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:55.868
Distractor.

16
00:00:56.617 --> 00:00:57.618
Synonym.

17
00:00:58.617 --> 00:01:01.406
Synonym means a word with a similar meaning.

18
00:01:02.017 --> 00:01:04.028
Purchase is a synonym of buy.

19
00:01:04.617 --> 00:01:07.176
Your turn. Say: Synonym.

20
00:01:10.033 --> 00:01:11.011
Synonym.

21
00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:12.867
Repetition.

22
00:01:13.883 --> 00:01:16.312
Repetition means hearing the same word again.

23
00:01:16.917 --> 00:01:18.742
Repetition can be a trap.

24
00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:22.281
Your turn. Say: Repetition.

25
00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:26.251
Repetition.

26
00:01:27.017 --> 00:01:28.285
Similar sound.

27
00:01:29.283 --> 00:01:31.887
Similar sound means words that sound alike.

28
00:01:32.483 --> 00:01:34.529
Right and write are similar sounds.

29
00:01:35.117 --> 00:01:37.711
Your turn. Say: Similar sound.

30
00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.090
Similar sound.

31
00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:44.257
Time reference.

32
00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:47.749
Time reference means a word that shows when.

33
00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:50.431
Listen for the time reference.

34
00:01:51.017 --> 00:01:53.878
Your turn. Say: Time reference.

35
00:01:56.733 --> 00:01:58.106
Time reference.

36
00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:00.025
Eliminate.

37
00:02:01.017 --> 00:02:03.573
Eliminate means to remove wrong options.

38
00:02:04.183 --> 00:02:05.846
Eliminate wrong answers.

39
00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.708
Your turn. Say: Eliminate.

40
00:02:11.567 --> 00:02:12.545
Eliminate.

41
00:02:13.283 --> 00:02:14.261
Review.

42
00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:16.913
Review means to check again.

43
00:02:17.517 --> 00:02:19.110
Review your mistakes.

44
00:02:19.717 --> 00:02:21.928
Your turn. Say: Review.

45
00:02:24.767 --> 00:02:25.861
Review.

46
00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:30.584
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:34.402
Visal, what is paraphrase in TOEIC Listening?

48
00:02:35.517 --> 00:02:46.493
The correct answer often says the same idea with different words. If the speaker says the shipment will be late, the answer may say the delivery is delayed.

49
00:02:47.583 --> 00:02:49.397
What are common distractors?

50
00:02:50.483 --> 00:03:00.947
Distractors repeat a word from the audio but change the meaning, use a similar sound, or describe the wrong time, such as last week instead of next week.

51
00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:03.260
How do I improve?

52
00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:12.343
Review each mistake and ask why the wrong option looked attractive. Make a list of paraphrases and practise listening with transcripts.

53
00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.116
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:20.794
Grammar focus: Strategy: choose meaning over matching words.

55
00:03:21.094 --> 00:03:22.258
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:25.739
The shipment will be late means the delivery is delayed.

57
00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:30.612
A word heard in the audio may be a distractor if the meaning changes.

58
00:03:31.567 --> 00:03:38.361
Expect paraphrase, avoid options that only repeat words, and review mistakes to learn which traps work on you.

59
00:03:39.117 --> 00:03:43.116
Be careful! Don't say: I choose the option with the same word.

60
00:03:45.067 --> 00:03:47.008
Say: I choose the same meaning.

61
00:03:47.308 --> 00:03:48.785
Meaning over words.

62
00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:52.252
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:54.497
Learning from Mistakes.

64
00:03:54.797 --> 00:03:57.447
Thida reviews her wrong answers in a notebook.

65
00:03:58.433 --> 00:04:01.907
She sees that she often chooses options with repeated words.

66
00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:06.095
Her teacher shows her that the right answer is a paraphrase.

67
00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:09.854
She makes a list of synonyms and paraphrases.

68
00:04:10.867 --> 00:04:13.342
In her next test she avoids the traps.

69
00:04:14.433 --> 00:04:18.284
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:20.859
A paraphrase uses blank.

71
00:04:21.159 --> 00:04:26.728
A, no words. B, different words for the same idea. C, the same words.

72
00:04:30.267 --> 00:04:33.323
The answer is B: different words for the same idea.

73
00:04:34.483 --> 00:04:36.878
A distractor may repeat a word but blank.

74
00:04:37.178 --> 00:04:41.237
A, be correct. B, be silent. C, change the meaning.

75
00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:47.345
The answer is C: change the meaning.

76
00:04:48.483 --> 00:04:50.622
The shipment will be late means blank.

77
00:04:50.922 --> 00:04:56.445
A, the delivery is delayed. B, the delivery is early. C, it is free.

78
00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.766
The answer is A: the delivery is delayed.

79
00:05:03.917 --> 00:05:05.405
What does Thida keep?

80
00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:10.508
A, a map. B, a mistake notebook. C, a diary of food.

81
00:05:14.067 --> 00:05:16.716
The answer is B: a mistake notebook.

82
00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.153
What should you choose?

83
00:05:19.453 --> 00:05:24.523
A, the repeated word. B, the longest option. C, the matching meaning.

84
00:05:28.067 --> 00:05:30.891
The answer is C: the matching meaning.

85
00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:35.437
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:36.283 --> 00:05:38.759
How do you avoid distractors in TOEIC Listening?

87
00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:48.992
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:49.292 --> 00:06:02.779
I listen for the meaning, not for the same words. I expect that correct answers use synonyms and paraphrases. After practice tests I review my mistakes and write down the traps that I fell into.

89
00:06:03.079 --> 00:06:04.789
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:05.683 --> 00:06:11.819
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: choose meaning over matching words.

91
00:06:12.119 --> 00:06:16.083
Today's value is reflection. Think about what you learned and how you grew.

92
00:06:16.383 --> 00:06:18.919
See you in Unit eleven. Goodbye!

93
00:06:19.219 --> 00:06:22.916
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

